      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we should only use node-\u003ethread for async transactions, or make it configurable whether it\u0027s used for async or both async and sync. Just using it for async allows userspace to still have multiple threads for an interface in the threadpool with RT prio inheritance (using rt_mutex), and at the same time have a dedicated RT thread for handling async transactions (which are anyway serialized).",
      "range": {
